From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 19:03:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: Optionally chain a render with a
 stamp-only wait

About one render.light command in four names its immediate predecessor
(a barrier or prior in its submission). The host publishes such a
command only once the predecessor has retired, so the render queue
drains every few commands, and fewer than three of the eight resident
units are busy on average. g16_render_chain 1 publishes the command
early instead, with a firmware wait for the previous render's FS, but
that wait uses the strict prior-command edge and the throughput does
not change.

Each FS already waits for its own TA with a stamp-only barrier, and
starts about 20 us after it. Add g16_render_chain 2: the same early
publication with the TA's wait for the previous FS encoded as a
stamp-only barrier. 0 and 1 are unchanged, and the default stays 0.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/engine.rs | 8 +++++++-
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs | 8 +++++++-
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/engine.rs b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/engine.rs
index 18669cd41b..5f28eb3c86 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/engine.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/engine.rs
@@ -2065,13 +2065,19 @@ fn prefix_render(
         // after the previous render's FS stamp (FS event 0x71), as the G15 backend's predecessor
         // barrier does; the previous render is the last one published (pf.draw).
         if params::render_chain() && job.own_wait_pending(job.progress.sent()) {
+            // g16_render_chain 2: a stamp-only wait, as the FS's own wait for its TA.
+            let ty = if params::render_chain_stamp() {
+                BarrierType::Stamp
+            } else {
+                BarrierType::Hold
+            };
             let prev = encode::barrier(
                 r.fw_stamp[1].va,
                 encode::stamp(pf.draw),
                 0x71,
                 target,
                 refs.uuid,
-                BarrierType::Hold,
+                ty,
             );
             p.prev_barrier.write(0, &prev)?;
             r.ring[0].w64(8 * pf.ta_head as usize, p.prev_barrier.va)?;
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
index b8049788f7..26ae01ddc6 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
@@ -914,13 +914,19 @@ pub(crate) fn render_chain() -> bool {
     RENDER_CHAIN.load(Ordering::Relaxed) != 0
 }
 
+/// `g16_render_chain` 2: the TA's wait for the previous render's FS is a stamp-only barrier,
+/// the type each FS already uses to wait for its own TA, instead of the strict edge (1).
+pub(crate) fn render_chain_stamp() -> bool {
+    RENDER_CHAIN.load(Ordering::Relaxed) == 2
+}
+
 live_u32_param!(
     RENDER_CHAIN_PARAM,
     RENDER_CHAIN_PARMTYPE,
     RENDER_CHAIN_PARM,
     RENDER_CHAIN,
     "g16_render_chain",
-    "G16: publish a render whose wait is on renders already published ahead of it, behind them, with a firmware wait for the previous FS (default 0: the host waits for their retirement; 1: firmware wait; runtime 0644)"
+    "G16: publish a render whose wait is on renders already published ahead of it, behind them, with a firmware wait for the previous FS (default 0: the host waits for their retirement; 1: firmware wait, strict edge; 2: firmware wait, stamp only; runtime 0644)"
 );
 
 /// Storage of `g16_fs_sample_size` (runtime 0644, default 0).
-- 
2.43.0

